WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.100
Speaker 1: I don't often talk about this on
the show, but I've mentioned off and on that

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:13.560
I've owned bitcoin for a long time and over
the last 24 hours I got like 10 or 12 different

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.849
requests to talk about what's going on with
bitcoin.

00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:22.369
And it's in the news so much in the last day
or two that I think it does make sense to

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:23.369
talk about it.

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:29.699
In the last week, we've seen some major mainstreaming
of bitcoin.

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:36.210
And at this point, the idea that it's just
going to go away is seeming very, very unlikely

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.210
to me.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.809
And I'm going to explain to you why.

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:44.359
But to give you some examples of the mainstreaming
of bitcoin recently, here is, for example,

00:00:44.359 --> 00:00:51.340
AMC Entertainment, which owns movie theaters
CEO Adam Aron, who says they are going to

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:56.309
start accepting Bitcoin, Litecoin and Ethereum
before the end of the year.

00:00:56.309 --> 00:00:57.720
And Dogecoin next year.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.720
Take a look at this.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.940
Speaker 4: Yeah, we've said we're going to
have that.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.420
We're going to accept before year end.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:07.910
We will accept Bitcoin, Litecoin, Ethereum,
Dogecoin all by here.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:11.920
All all, buy right now for the gift card.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:12.990
By year end.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.890
Four Bitcoin Litecoin in theory.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.110
Well, I think we'll be able to take Dogecoin
in Q1.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:23.200
So again, big changes, we're we're entering
the 21st century in a big way.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.439
Speaker 1: We've also learned over time and
some of these decisions were actually made

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:34.399
made long ago about how more and more college
endowments, as well as financial advisory

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:39.850
type companies are holding or recommending
holding some percentage of assets in cryptocurrency.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:46.050
Some examples the Harvard management company
has invested in bitcoin since 2019, according

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.710
to one report.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:57.130
The Brown University Endowment has invested
in cryptocurrency now for some period of time.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:03.729
JPMorgan is now or has been since about six
months ago, suggesting to investors, Maybe

00:02:03.729 --> 00:02:09.039
look at putting one percent of your portfolio
in bitcoin.

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:15.340
Morgan Stanley has actually started offering
its wealthy clients access to bitcoin funds,

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:21.780
and a number of new funds and ETFs have gone
live even in the last several weeks, just

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.860
picking different things to show you the breadth
of this.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:34.000
NBA owner Mark Cuban says that soon the Mavericks
will accept Dogecoin for tickets to the games,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.659
and the Mavericks have long been asset long
for some period of time have already been

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:42.069
accepting bitcoin for payment as well.

00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:47.410
So all of these things together, what what
is the point here, I guess, is the question.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:52.960
This is not a segment about is bitcoin good
or is bitcoin bad?

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:58.409
In fact, the the longer bitcoin is around,
it's sort of like saying, is the dollar good

00:02:58.409 --> 00:02:59.910
or is the dollar bad?

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:03.819
These are financial technologies that exist.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:06.030
And really, it's about how were they used?

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.150
How are they regulated?

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:08.900
What do they mean, etc.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.170
This is not about is bitcoin used for criminal
transactions?

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.700
Sure, it is.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.459
The dollar is still the primary currency used
for criminal transactions.

00:03:17.459 --> 00:03:20.700
Not a super interesting conversation for this
segment.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.000
What about energy use for bitcoin mining?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.670
An important topic for sure.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.470
Not the topic of this particular conversation.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:34.739
The conversation today is is this going to
be merely a passing fad?

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:39.390
And it seems tougher and tougher to argue
that bitcoin is going to be a passing fad.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:45.470
Now, notice that I haven't talked in this
segment about the price of bitcoin yesterday

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:46.470
today.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:54.890
Bitcoin roughly equaled its all time high
of about $64000 per coin.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:59.380
This is about adoption and this is about use.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.990
It's tough to imagine bitcoin just evaporating.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:06.430
Could it be regulated into obscurity at this
point?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.800
Maybe, maybe.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.689
But it would really require coordinated action
by lots of governments.

00:04:11.689 --> 00:04:13.480
And even then, I'm unsure.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:19.900
There are ETFs, there are funds, mainstream
funds and ETFs which are based on cryptocurrency

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.400
at this point in time.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.380
Now am I recommending anyone do anything in
particular?

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.220
Absolutely not.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:28.590
That's not what the show is about.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:34.060
This is not a segment about buy bitcoin or
sell bitcoin, or I think bitcoin will be worth

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.700
X at any point in time.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.190
That's not it at all.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:42.630
I wondered if this might be something with
lasting potential.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:48.600
Back in 2015, and so I bought bitcoin back
then in a few other coins, and as they've

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:55.510
gone up in value, I've sold pieces of my holdings
to lock in gains, all with the idea that I

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.240
have no idea where this is going to go.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.670
But now?

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:06.880
My thinking is as follows Nassim Nicholas
Taleb wrote the book, The Black Swan, wrote

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.340
the book Antifragile, as well as other books.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.590
Very interesting work, Nassim Nicholas Taleb.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:17.850
And he says, you know, when thinking about
like, for example, what books to read and

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:22.950
what has stood the test of time and likely
will continue to, he says.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:27.270
You know, if something's been around for 500
years and people keep reading it, it's quite

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.670
plausible that it's going to be around and
people are going to keep reading it for another

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:31.960
500 years.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.990
That might be something worth reading.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:38.240
Maybe if the topic is interesting and you
know, everybody make a decision for yourself,

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:45.210
a book that's been around for a year, we can
say it'll probably be around another year.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:48.910
But it's harder to say it'll probably be around
another 500 years.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:53.600
And in fact, most books written in the last
year are not going to be read 500 years from

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.070
now.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:06:00.260
Along the same lines, bitcoin was created
in 2009.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.950
That's now been 12 almost 13 years.

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:06.850
It's hard to imagine it going poof in the
next month.

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:10.600
It's hard to imagine it going poof in the
next year.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:18.900
And so the longer that it goes, particularly
when you see trade volumes so high and the

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:25.320
price is certainly a signal as well, it becomes
more and more reasonable to think it's going

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.760
to continue being around.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:33.830
And that's a really interesting change from
what was being said in 2011 and what was being

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.420
said in 2013.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:40.610
So again, just to be really, really clear,
I have no idea what the price of bitcoin is

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:41.900
going to be.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:48.580
I'm not suggesting anyone buy or sell it,
but at this point, as a financial technology,

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.460
it seems as though it's here to stay.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:56.390
And it's quite plausible that it's been here
almost 12, almost 13 years.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.390
It's quite plausible to me.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.750
It's going to be around another 12 or 13 years.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.790
At that point, it will be 26 years.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:06.840
And if it can make it that long, it becomes
even harder to imagine that it's just going

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.020
to disappear.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:10.590
That's my perspective at this point in time.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:17.490
I'm curious to hear from folks and please
comment on what I've actually said, which

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:20.090
has nothing to do with what I expect the price
of bitcoin to be.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:21.500
I've not said a word about that

